      "claim": "In humans, 18F-mefway entered the brain quickly with a peak SUV of 1.7, providing direct clinical evidence of meaningful CNS access.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple independent in vivo studies across mice, rats, monkeys, and humans consistently demonstrate rapid and meaningful brain uptake after systemic administration. No contradictory direct CNS-access evidence was retrieved.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "Quantitative plasma-to-brain ratios or unbound brain concentrations are not consistently reported, but direct brain uptake and PET evidence is sufficient to support meaningful CNS access."
  ],
